<title>MEXICO: Mexico gives breakdown of pension commissions.</title>
<headline>Mexico gives breakdown of pension commissions.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-02-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's National Retirement Savings System Commission issued the following breakdown of maximum principal commissions registered by approved pension fund management firms, or Afores as they are known in Mexico:</p>
<p>			COMMISSIONS</p>
<p>			  (Pct)</p>
<p>AFORE	  On	 On	   On Real</p>
<p>		 Flows    Balance    Return</p>
<p>Banamex	1.70</p>
<p>Bancomer     1.70</p>
<p>Banorte	1.00     1.50</p>
<p>Bital	  1.21     3.50</p>
<p>Garante	1.77     0.70</p>
<p>Genesis	1.70     0.65</p>
<p>Inbursa				   33.00</p>
<p>Previnter    1.60</p>
<p>Profuturo-</p>
<p>GNP	    1.98     0.36</p>
<p>Santander-</p>
<p>Mexicano     1.99     1.00</p>
<p>Tepeyac	1.17     1.00</p>
<p>((-- Henry Tricks, Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9560))</p>
